@startuml mock-ui-feedback-loop
!theme plain
title Mock UI Feedback Loop (zoom-in on Roadmap Stage 1 — see docs/06-roadmap.md)

start

repeat
  :Build/update mock UI screens
  against docs/02-v1-scope.md;
  note right: Static mock data + mock auth,\nno backend dependency (docs/05-ui-ux-plan.md)

  :Run tsc / lint / production build
  (catch anything before it reaches reviewers);

  :Deploy to Vercel;

  :Share link with reviewers
  (friends first, wider circle later);
  note right
    Tell reviewers what's mock vs. real,
    and point them at already-known gaps
    (docs/07-future-scope.md,
    05-ui-ux-plan.md "Assumptions & Open Questions")
    so feedback focuses on new findings.
  end note

  :Collect concrete feedback
  (specific screens/flows, not just impressions);

  if (UX/UI fix within current scope?) then (yes)
    :Fix directly in mock UI;
  else (product-direction question)
    :Raise explicitly, decide,
    update docs/02-v1-scope.md
    or docs/07-future-scope.md;
  endif
repeat while (More significant feedback to act on?) is (yes) not (no)

:Sign off on mock UI
(Roadmap Stage 1 complete);

stop

@enduml
